= szkola_izba
# tlo: szkola_izba
The school was housed in a wooden building – a single room with two windows, a great tiled stove in the corner and benches so worn that their tops were covered with initials carved by the penknives of several generations. It smelled of chalk, wet wool and smoke.
Mr Ignacy was old and thin; he limped on his right leg and wore wire-rimmed spectacles that kept slipping down to the tip of his nose. His voice was quiet, but when he raised it, the whole room fell silent. He taught everything at once: writing, sums, catechism and hymns. In his desk drawer he kept a thick, leather-bound notebook which he showed to no one.
From the very first day Jaromir loved the letters. They looked like little people – some stood on one leg, others spread their arms, still others stooped like the old beggars by the wayside shrine – and you only had to set them side by side for them to start making words. Hanka, for her part, was best at sums, and Antek sang beautifully, though no one had known it before, because at home he was too shy to open his mouth.
Not that it was always sweet and pleasant. In Bukowiec lived Bartek, the miller’s son – taller than Franek, with fists like loaves and a look of everlasting boredom. He had singled out Antek. He mocked his patched breeches, hid his cap, and at break stuck out a foot to trip him whenever he went past.
One day, when Mr Ignacy had stepped out of the room for a moment, Bartek snatched the boy’s slate and began rubbing out with his sleeve the letters Antek had been writing all morning. Antek stood there with red ears and clenched fists, and tears in his eyes. # pokaz: bartek
# pytanie: How will Jaromir act?
*   [Stand up for Antek.]
    ~ obrona_antka = stanal
    “Give it back to him,” said Jaromir, and was surprised himself at how calm it sounded.
    Bartek turned slowly, in disbelief, as if a bench had spoken to him. Then he laughed and shoved him so hard that he flew against the stove. But Jaromir got up. He fell and got up again. The third time, Franek was already standing beside him, and behind Franek – which no one had expected – Hanka, with a split of kindling in her hand. The miller’s son returned the slate, spat at their feet and slouched back to his bench. # pokaz: obrona
    Jaromir was left with a lump on his forehead and a cut lip, and Mr Ignacy, who turned up just at the end, made both him and Bartek kneel in the corner until the bell. But on the way home Antek walked beside him instead of behind, as he usually did, and said nothing, only glanced sideways at him now and then. # pokaz: ignacy # dalej
