= sosna_spirala
# tlo: sosna_spirala
~ zapiski += pan_lasu_1
On the way back, at the edge of the forest, Hanka stopped mid-step.
“Look.”
On a thick pine right by the path, the bark had been stripped. Not in the ordinary way deer or wild boar tear it, but neatly, in a narrow band that wound round the trunk in a spiral from the very ground up to the first branches. Beneath it showed pale, damp wood, and in a few places drops of fresh resin ran down it, thick and glistening like tears.
“Deer,” said Antek, more to himself than to the others.
Jaromir went closer. The spiral was too even and too careful for any animal to have made it. At the very bottom, by the ground, lay a torn-off piece of bark – curled into a little tube, still smelling of the forest.
