In November the days grew short and grey, and the evenings long. Mud mixed with leaves squelched underfoot, the wind tore at the bare branches, and everything around smelled of damp and rot. The boy now came home from school after dark, and the whole way along the edge of the forest he walked with his eyes fixed on the path, saying Hail Marys in his head so as not to hear whether anyone among the trees was counting.
