= wieczory_jesienia
{ figurka_u_staruchy:
    More and more often his father sat on the threshold in the evenings with a pipe that kept going out. When once his son asked him whether he believed in the Lord of the Forest, he turned on him so sharply that the boy stepped back. Yet his father said nothing. He got up and went to bed, and in the night Jaromir heard him pacing the room for a long time.
- else:
    When his father heard about the Lord of the Forest at supper, he laughed and said that if Borowy came, he’d get a bowl of groats and be packed off to sleep on the stove. But afterwards he stared out of the window for a long while, and before he lay down he stood the axe in the passage by the door, which he had never done before.
}
On the night from Sunday to Monday the first snow fell. Jaromir woke before dawn because the room had grown strangely bright, and went to the window. # pokaz: snieg
The world was white and silent. A soft down lay on the fence, on the barn roof, on the branches of the apple tree.
He stood at the cold pane for a long time, looking towards the forest, until his fingers went numb on the sill, and he could not make himself go back under the featherbed. # dalej
